# Update FUNCTIONAL_FLOW.md for every feature

When adding or changing a **user-facing flow**, **API endpoint**, or **module**, update [`docs/FUNCTIONAL_FLOW.md`](../../docs/FUNCTIONAL_FLOW.md) in the same change.

## Required updates

1. **Sections 1–3** — Add or revise the numbered flow (steps: Page → action → API → DB → outcome). Tag status: ✅ complete, ⚠️ partial, ❌ missing, ⏭️ deferred/skipped.
2. **Section 7** — Mark the module item (e.g. `A-M6`) in the completion tables with the correct icon.
3. **Section 5** — Update the gap matrix row when a layer (Web UI, API, DB, Admin UI, Notify) changes.
4. **Section 8** — Append an implementation-log entry with date and touched files.

## Status icons (use consistently)

| Icon | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| ✅ | Complete end-to-end |
| ⚠️ | Partial / stubbed |
| ❌ | Missing |
| ⏭️ | Deferred or explicitly skipped |

## Example (Section 8 log row)

`| A-M6 | Share / deep link on business profile | \`BusinessDetail.tsx\` — copy link + WhatsApp |`

Do not ship new routes, pages, or modules without updating this doc.
